<% content_for :title, "AgEvidence Developer OS" %>

<section class="page-header">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">Developer operating system</p>
    <h1>From source record to reliance artifact</h1>
    <p class="lead">Start with a signed operational event or a controlled source reference, then move through extraction, review, pricing, artifact assembly, and local verification.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="d-flex gap-2 flex-wrap">
    <%= link_to "Create project", new_agevidence_developer_project_path, class: "btn btn-primary" %>
    <%= link_to "Event inbox", integrations_events_path, class: "btn btn-outline-primary" %>
    <%= link_to "API contract", agevidence_developer_os_openapi_path, class: "btn btn-outline-secondary" %>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="alert alert-boundary">
  One bridge, two entry paths. The existing Athian platform remains authoritative for operations; Rails preserves event and source projections, and portable receipts remain independently verifiable.
</div>

<section class="dashboard-grid">
  <article class="metric-card">
    <span class="metric-label">Inbox events</span>
    <strong><%= @inbox_counts.fetch(:events) %></strong>
    <small>Signed operational inputs</small>
  </article>
  <article class="metric-card">
    <span class="metric-label">Evidence projections</span>
    <strong><%= @inbox_counts.fetch(:projections) %></strong>
    <small>Append-only Rails state</small>
  </article>
  <article class="metric-card">
    <span class="metric-label">Receipt outbox</span>
    <strong><%= @inbox_counts.fetch(:outbox) %></strong>
    <small>Async trust-boundary requests</small>
  </article>
  <article class="metric-card">
    <span class="metric-label">Result callbacks</span>
    <strong><%= @inbox_counts.fetch(:deliveries) %></strong>
    <small>Artifact and reliance notifications</small>
  </article>
</section>

<section class="content-section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Start here</p>
      <h2>Dual-path launchpad</h2>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="row g-3">
    <div class="col-lg-6">
      <article class="resource-card h-100">
        <span class="badge text-bg-dark">Event Inbox Path</span>
        <h3 class="mt-3">Existing Athian operational events</h3>
        <p>Publish eight signed material events into <code>POST /v1/integrations/events</code>. The inbox accepts quickly, maps upstream IDs, creates projections, and sends receipt work to the outbox.</p>
        <div class="code-panel">
<pre class="mb-0"><code>curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/v1/integrations/events \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "X-Athian-Integration-Source: athian_salesforce_production" \
  -H "X-Athian-Timestamp: 2026-08-04T18:42:11Z" \
  -H "X-Athian-Signature: v1=&lt;signature&gt;" \
  --data @examples/integrations/project_4030_beef/01-project.registered.json</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="d-flex gap-2 mt-3">
          <%= link_to "Inspect inbox", integrations_events_path, class: "btn btn-sm btn-primary" %>
          <%= link_to "Operations", integrations_operations_path, class: "btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" %>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="col-lg-6">
      <article class="resource-card h-100">
        <span class="badge text-bg-success">Source Records Path</span>
        <h3 class="mt-3">Startup-controlled source references</h3>
        <p>Create a project, submit controlled references, run fixture-backed extraction, append human review decisions, and request a priced reliance artifact.</p>
        <div class="code-panel">
<pre class="mb-0"><code>curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/v1/developer/projects \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  --data '{"developer_account":{"name":"Northstar Methane Systems Sandbox"},"project":{"name":"Enterprise dairy pilot","target_claim":"The intervention reduces enteric methane."}}'</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="d-flex gap-2 mt-3">
          <%= link_to "New project", new_agevidence_developer_project_path, class: "btn btn-sm btn-primary" %>
          <%= link_to "All projects", agevidence_developer_projects_path, class: "btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" %>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="content-section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Sandbox projects</p>
      <h2>Evidence maps ready for developer workflow</h2>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="table-responsive">
    <table class="table align-middle">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Startup</th>
          <th>Project</th>
          <th>Sources</th>
          <th>Runs</th>
          <th>Orders</th>
          <th></th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% @projects.each do |project| %>
          <tr>
            <td><%= project.developer_account.name %></td>
            <td><%= project.name %></td>
            <td><%= project.source_records.size %></td>
            <td><%= project.model_runs.size %></td>
            <td><%= project.artifact_orders.size %></td>
            <td class="text-end"><%= link_to "Open OS", agevidence_developer_project_path(project), class: "btn btn-sm btn-primary" %></td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="content-section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Project 4030 fixture runner</p>
      <h2>One-click current-business bridge scaffold</h2>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p>The canonical fixture sequence is intentionally limited to the implemented eight-event vocabulary. Future livestock events stay deferred until a paid mapping requires them.</p>
  <div class="row g-2">
    <% @project_4030_events.each do |event_file| %>
      <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-3">
        <div class="resource-card h-100">
          <code><%= event_file %></code>
        </div>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <div class="code-panel mt-3">
<pre class="mb-0"><code>ruby examples/integrations/project_4030_beef/replay_project_4030.rb \
  http://localhost:3000 athian_salesforce_production "$ATHIAN_INTEGRATION_SECRET"</code></pre>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="content-section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Commercial sandbox</p>
      <h2>Quote, order, assemble, verify</h2>
    </div>
    <span class="small text-muted"><%= @product_notice %></span>
  </div>
  <div class="row g-3">
    <% @products.each do |code, product| %>
      <div class="col-md-6 col-xl-4">
        <article class="resource-card h-100">
          <h3><%= product.fetch("name") %></h3>
          <p><%= product.fetch("description") %></p>
          <div class="d-flex justify-content-between">
            <span class="badge text-bg-secondary"><%= product.fetch("billing_type").humanize %></span>
            <strong><%= money(product.fetch("base_planning_price_cents") / 100.0) %></strong>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="content-section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">SDK snippets</p>
      <h2>Same contract from Python or TypeScript</h2>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="row g-3">
    <div class="col-lg-6">
      <div class="code-panel h-100">
<pre class="mb-0"><code>from agevidence_client import AgEvidenceClient

client = AgEvidenceClient("http://localhost:3000")
project = client.create_project(
    account_name="Northstar Methane Systems Sandbox",
    project_name="Enterprise dairy pilot",
    target_claim="The intervention reduces enteric methane.",
)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col-lg-6">
      <div class="code-panel h-100">
<pre class="mb-0"><code>const client = new AgEvidenceClient("http://localhost:3000");
const project = await client.createProject({
  accountName: "Northstar Methane Systems Sandbox",
  projectName: "Enterprise dairy pilot",
  targetClaim: "The intervention reduces enteric methane."
});</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="content-section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Webhook tester</p>
      <h2>Signed result callbacks</h2>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p>Register endpoints under <code>/v1/integrations/webhook_endpoints</code>. Result payloads stay small: artifact ID, receipt root, verification state, compatibility state, reliance state, download metadata, and the local verifier command.</p>
</section>
